// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 05.1 ■ ENTRY VOLATILITY FILTER
// The single condition that separated the winning stretches from the bleeding
// ones. Quiet candles are where this line's touches mean something; once ATR
// runs hot, a touch is just noise and the fixed stop is reached before the
// fixed target. The filter blocks new entries only — an open trade keeps its
// stop and target and is never closed by it.
//
// The working band is wide — every ceiling from 25 to 45 points beat no filter
// — so the effect is real even though the exact best value inside that band is
// noise. Below 25 the filter starts removing good trades along with the bad.
//
// One caveat worth knowing: this threshold is an absolute number of points,
// calibrated against gold trading between 4,000 and 5,600. A much higher or
// lower price level moves typical ATR with it, and the number would need
// rescaling rather than trusting.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
useVolFilter = input.bool(true, "Block Entries When Volatility Is High", group=G_VOL, tooltip="Measured on Jan-Jul 2026 XAUUSD. Off: 7,687 trades, +837 points, worst drawdown 10,839, three of seven months positive. On: 3,575 trades, +9,568 points, worst drawdown 3,889, all seven months positive. It costs about half the trade count.")
volAtrLength = input.int(14, "Filter ATR Length", minval=1, group=G_VOL)
maxEntryAtrPoints = input.float(26.0, "Maximum Entry ATR (Points)", minval=1.0, step=1.0, group=G_VOL, tooltip="Entries are blocked above this. Every value from 25 to 45 tested better than no filter; 26 measured best, but the differences inside that band are within noise, so treat it as a region rather than a precise setting.")
minEntryAtrPoints = input.float(0.0, "Minimum Entry ATR (Points)", minval=0.0, step=1.0, group=G_VOL, tooltip="Blocks entries in a dead market. Left at 0 by default because a floor did not improve the measured result.")

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
